Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:05:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(elero_web): copy packet JSON without the async
 clipboard API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`navigator.clipboard` is only defined on secure origins. The gateway is
served over plain HTTP on a LAN address, so the copy button in the RF packet
table always threw:

    Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'writeText')

It could therefore never work on a real device — only on localhost or behind
a TLS proxy.

Add a `copyText()` helper that uses `navigator.clipboard` when it exists and
otherwise falls back to a hidden textarea plus `document.execCommand('copy')`,
restoring any prior selection. It reports success, so the button now shows an
error toast instead of silently doing nothing when both paths fail.

Source only — `elero_web_ui.h` is a release artifact and is rebuilt by CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
